Deniz S Yasar (yasar@cs.ucdavis.edu) wrote:
: I have noticed some posters have made reference to bones levels and
: dying and coming back to levels with new characters.  This never
: happens to me, if I die, nethack generates a new dungeon, and
: supposedly new persona monsters, am I missing something, and what
: exactly are bones levels, I noticed data files for them in the lib
: directory, but they are not intelligible.

When you die, sometimes (always?) the game will generate a bones
file for the level you died on.  When another character gets to
that level, sometimes (not always, I know) the game will access
that bones file.  The level will be identical to the one you 
died on, with all the monsters that killed you the first time.
Where you were standing will be a ghost of you on a pile of all
your old equipment, except that artifacts you had in the old
game and have already been created in the new will just be normal
weapons, and much of the stuff will be cursed.  It is a good way
to get lots of good stuff, and also to die while carrying it
around.  If you rob a shop, and get killed, and the bones file
from that level (the one with the shop) is used, the shopkeeper
will still be hostile (if you have the same name (and class?)
as the old game).  They're lots of fun on multi-user systems,
and a big pain on all systems.  I wish they'd be compiled out
on PC systems, as I've had the same bones level kill me seven
games in a row (gnomish mines, with a polymorph trap, and more
nastier monsters than even the castle ever had).  Eventually,
I just deleted it.

